---
import PlaygroundShell from '../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Simulate it" hint="A sorted list is searched four ways and every look at an item (a probe) is counted, never timed. The list is generated by a formula, so the numbers never change. The list of values is odd numbers only, each repeated as many times as you choose, so the value 2 is always missing.">
  <ol class="how">
    <li>Set <b>Items n</b> to <b>1,000,000</b>, <b>Copies of each value</b> to <b>1</b> and <b>Target</b> to <b>Last value</b>: the linear scan makes <b>1,000,000</b> probes, binary search <b>20</b> and the lower-bound version <b>21</b>. Halving costs about log2 n, so a thousand times more items cost only about ten more probes.</li>
    <li>Set <b>Items n</b> to <b>1,000</b>, <b>Copies of each value</b> to <b>4</b> and <b>Target</b> to <b>First value</b>: binary search stops early but reports a later copy (index 2), the lower-bound version needs <b>11</b> probes and reports index 0, the first copy. Set <b>Target</b> to <b>Last value</b>: the <b>lo = mid</b> version is stuck and gives up at <b>64</b> probes, although it was fine for the first value.</li>
    <li>In the box <b>The midpoint in 32-bit integers</b>, set <b>Search range</b> to <b>1,500,000,000 to 2,000,000,000</b>: the sum wraps to <b>-794,967,296</b>, the naive midpoint is <b>-397,483,648</b> and the safe one is <b>1,750,000,000</b>.</li>
    <li>In the box <b>Searching an answer space</b>, set <b>Packages</b> to <b>1,000</b> and <b>Days</b> to <b>3</b>: the smallest capacity is <b>3,503</b>, found with <b>13</b> checks (<b>13,000</b> steps). Counting up from the heaviest package needs <b>3,484</b> checks (<b>3,484,000</b> steps).</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="pg bs" data-bs>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Items n <select class="pg-in" data-n><option value="10">10</option><option value="100">100</option><option value="1000" selected>1,000</option><option value="10000">10,000</option><option value="1000000">1,000,000</option></select></label>
      <label>Copies of each value <select class="pg-in" data-run><option value="1" selected>1</option><option value="4">4</option><option value="50">50</option></select></label>
      <label>Target <select class="pg-in" data-target><option value="first">First value</option><option value="last" selected>Last value</option><option value="middle">Middle value</option><option value="missing">A missing value</option></select></label>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" data-b1><h3>Linear scan</h3><span class="pg-mono bs-big" data-o1></span><span class="pg-note" data-n1></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b2><h3>Binary search, stop at any match</h3><span class="pg-mono bs-big" data-o2></span><span class="pg-note" data-n2></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b3><h3>Binary search, first match (lower bound)</h3><span class="pg-mono bs-big" data-o3></span><span class="pg-note" data-n3></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b4><h3>Binary search with lo = mid</h3><span class="pg-mono bs-big" data-o4></span><span class="pg-note" data-n4></span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--border)">
      <h3>Probes, log scale</h3>
      <div class="bs-bars" data-bars></div>
      <span class="pg-note" data-verdict></span>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--border)">
      <h3>The midpoint in 32-bit integers</h3>
      <div class="pg-row"><label>Search range <select class="pg-in" data-range><option value="0">1,000,000,000 to 1,100,000,000</option><option value="1">1,500,000,000 to 2,000,000,000</option><option value="2">2,000,000,000 to 2,100,000,000</option></select></label></div>
      <div class="pg-grid">
        <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--border)"><h3>lo and hi</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-m1></span></div>
        <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--border)"><h3>(lo + hi) in 32 bits</h3><span class="pg-mono bs-big" data-m2></span></div>
        <div class="pg-box" data-mb3><h3>Naive midpoint</h3><span class="pg-mono bs-big" data-m3></span><span class="pg-note" data-m3n></span></div>
        <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--good)"><h3>Safe midpoint: lo + (hi - lo) / 2</h3><span class="pg-mono bs-big" data-m4></span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--border)">
      <h3>Searching an answer space</h3>
      <p class="pg-note">Packages must ship in order. Each day carries at most the ship's capacity. What is the smallest capacity that finishes in the given days? There is no array of answers: every capacity is tested by a pass over the packages, and "does it fit" only flips once as the capacity grows, so halving works.</p>
      <div class="pg-row">
        <label>Packages <select class="pg-in" data-pk><option value="100">100</option><option value="1000" selected>1,000</option></select></label>
        <label>Days <select class="pg-in" data-days><option value="3" selected>3</option><option value="10">10</option></select></label>
      </div>
      <div class="pg-grid">
        <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--border)"><h3>Smallest capacity</h3><span class="pg-mono bs-big" data-a1></span><span class="pg-note" data-a1n></span></div>
        <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--good)"><h3>Binary search on capacity</h3><span class="pg-mono bs-big" data-a2></span></div>
        <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--bad)"><h3>Counting up from the heaviest package</h3><span class="pg-mono bs-big" data-a3></span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<script>
  import { query, formatThousands } from '../playground';

  // The same model as the code samples: the list is a formula, nothing is stored.
  const CAP = 64;
  const half = (x: number) => Math.floor(x / 2);
  const at = (i: number, run: number) => Math.floor(i / run) * 2 + 1;
  const firstIndex = (v: number, run: number) => half(v - 1) * run;
  function linear(n: number, run: number, t: number): [number, number] {
    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) if (at(i, run) === t) return [i + 1, i];
    return [n, -1];
  }
  function binaryAny(n: number, run: number, t: number): [number, number] {
    let lo = 0, hi = n - 1, probes = 0;
    while (lo <= hi) {
      const mid = lo + half(hi - lo); probes++;
      const v = at(mid, run);
      if (v === t) return [probes, mid];
      if (v < t) lo = mid + 1; else hi = mid - 1;
    }
    return [probes, -1];
  }
  function lowerBound(n: number, run: number, t: number): [number, number] {
    let lo = 0, hi = n, probes = 0;
    while (lo < hi) { const mid = lo + half(hi - lo); probes++; if (at(mid, run) < t) lo = mid + 1; else hi = mid; }
    probes++;
    return lo < n && at(lo, run) === t ? [probes, lo] : [probes, -1];
  }
  function buggy(n: number, run: number, t: number): [number, boolean] {
    let lo = 0, hi = n - 1, probes = 0;
    while (lo < hi && probes < CAP) { const mid = lo + half(hi - lo); probes++; if (at(mid, run) < t) lo = mid; else hi = mid; }
    return [probes, lo < hi];
  }
  const weight = (i: number) => 1 + ((i * 37 + 11) % 20);
  function daysNeeded(n: number, cap: number): number {
    let days = 1, load = 0;
    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) { const w = weight(i); if (load + w > cap) { days++; load = 0; } load += w; }
    return days;
  }
  const RANGES: [number, number][] = [[1000000000, 1100000000], [1500000000, 2000000000], [2000000000, 2100000000]];

  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-bs]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = query(root);
    const colour = (id: string, c: string) => q<HTMLElement>(id).style.setProperty('--c', c);
    const sel = (s: string) => q<HTMLSelectElement>(s).value;
    function draw() {
      const n = Number(sel('[data-n]')), run = Number(sel('[data-run]')), which = sel('[data-target]');
      const t = which === 'first' ? at(0, run) : which === 'last' ? at(n - 1, run) : which === 'middle' ? at(half(n), run) : 2;
      const [lc, lp] = linear(n, run, t), [bc, bp] = binaryAny(n, run, t), [oc, op] = lowerBound(n, run, t), [gc, stuck] = buggy(n, run, t);
      const first = lp >= 0 ? firstIndex(t, run) : -1;
      q('[data-o1]').textContent = `${formatThousands(lc)} probes`;
      q('[data-n1]').textContent = lp < 0 ? 'looked at every item and found nothing' : `found index ${formatThousands(lp)}, the first copy: a scan from the left always finds it`;
      colour('[data-b1]', 'var(--border)');
      q('[data-o2]').textContent = `${formatThousands(bc)} probes`;
      q('[data-n2]').textContent = bp < 0 ? 'not found' : bp === first ? `index ${formatThousands(bp)}, the first copy` : `index ${formatThousands(bp)}, but the first copy is at index ${formatThousands(first)}: any match, not the first`;
      colour('[data-b2]', bp >= 0 && bp !== first ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--good)');
      q('[data-o3]').textContent = `${formatThousands(oc)} probes`;
      q('[data-n3]').textContent = op < 0 ? 'not found' : `index ${formatThousands(op)}, always the first copy; one extra probe to confirm the match`;
      colour('[data-b3]', 'var(--good)');
      q('[data-o4]').textContent = stuck ? `gave up at ${gc} probes` : `${formatThousands(gc)} probes`;
      q('[data-n4]').textContent = stuck ? 'stuck: lo and hi are neighbours, mid equals lo and nothing changes. The probe cap stopped it; without the cap it never ends' : 'finished this time: it only hangs when the last step is "move lo up"';
      colour('[data-b4]', stuck ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--good)');

      const bars = q('[data-bars]'); bars.textContent = '';
      const rows: [string, number][] = [['Linear scan', lc], ['Stop at any match', bc], ['First match', oc], ['lo = mid (capped)', gc]];
      const top = Math.log10(Math.max(...rows.map((r) => r[1]), 10));
      for (const [label, v] of rows) {
        const row = document.createElement('div'); row.className = 'bs-bar';
        const name = document.createElement('span'); name.textContent = label;
        const track = document.createElement('span'); track.className = 'bs-track';
        const fill = document.createElement('span'); fill.className = 'bs-fill'; fill.style.width = `${Math.max(2, (Math.log10(Math.max(1, v)) / top) * 100)}%`;
        track.appendChild(fill);
        const num = document.createElement('span'); num.className = 'pg-mono'; num.textContent = formatThousands(v);
        row.append(name, track, num); bars.appendChild(row);
      }
      const billion = 1000000000;
      q('[data-verdict]').textContent = `Halving needs about log2 n probes: ${formatThousands(n)} items need ${Math.floor(Math.log2(n)) + 1} at most, and ${formatThousands(billion)} items would need ${Math.floor(Math.log2(billion)) + 1}. A scan of ${formatThousands(billion)} items can need ${formatThousands(billion)}. Big O describes this growth, not the exact count.`;

      const [lo, hi] = RANGES[Number(sel('[data-range]'))];
      const s = (lo + hi) | 0, naive = half(s);
      q('[data-m1]').textContent = `lo=${formatThousands(lo)} hi=${formatThousands(hi)}`;
      q('[data-m2]').textContent = formatThousands(s);
      q('[data-m3]').textContent = formatThousands(naive);
      q('[data-m3n]').textContent = naive < lo ? 'wrong: below lo, the search would read outside its range' : 'fine here: the sum still fits in 32 bits';
      colour('[data-mb3]', naive < lo ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--good)');
      q('[data-m4]').textContent = formatThousands(lo + half(hi - lo));

      const pk = Number(sel('[data-pk]')), days = Number(sel('[data-days]'));
      let heaviest = 0, total = 0;
      for (let i = 0; i < pk; i++) { heaviest = Math.max(heaviest, weight(i)); total += weight(i); }
      let a = heaviest, b = total, probes = 0;
      while (a < b) { const mid = a + half(b - a); probes++; if (daysNeeded(pk, mid) <= days) b = mid; else a = mid + 1; }
      const tries = a - heaviest + 1;
      q('[data-a1]').textContent = formatThousands(a);
      q('[data-a1n]').textContent = `searched capacities ${formatThousands(heaviest)} to ${formatThousands(total)}`;
      q('[data-a2]').textContent = `${formatThousands(probes)} checks (${formatThousands(probes * pk)} steps)`;
      q('[data-a3]').textContent = `${formatThousands(tries)} checks (${formatThousands(tries * pk)} steps)`;
    }
    root.addEventListener('change', draw);
    draw();
  });
</script>
<style is:global>
  .playground .pg-mono { overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .playground label { max-width: 100%; }
  .playground select.pg-in { max-width: 100%; min-width: 0; width: 100%; }
  .playground .pg-row > label { min-width: 0; max-width: 100%; }
  .playground .bs-big { font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: 600; }
  .playground .bs-bars { display: grid; gap: 6px; }
  .playground .bs-bar { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 9.5rem 1fr; gap: 2px 8px; align-items: center; }
  .playground .bs-bar .pg-mono { grid-column: 2; }
  .playground .bs-track { display: block; height: 12px; border-radius: 6px; background: var(--surface-2); overflow: hidden; }
  .playground .bs-fill { display: block; height: 100%; background: var(--accent); border-radius: 6px; }
  @media (max-width: 520px) { .playground .bs-bar { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .playground .bs-bar .pg-mono { grid-column: 1; } }
</style>
